```go
// Slice — dynamic array (reference type)
s := []int{1, 2, 3}
s = append(s, 4, 5)
s = append(s, []int{6, 7, 8}...)

// Slicing
s[1:3]      // [2, 3]
s[:3]       // first 3
s[2:]       // from index 2
len(s)      // length
cap(s)      // capacity

// make — pre-allocate
sl  := make([]int, 5)      // len=5, cap=5, all zeros
sl2 := make([]int, 3, 10)  // len=3, cap=10

// copy
dst := make([]int, len(src))
copy(dst, src)

// 2D slice
matrix := [][]int{
    {1, 2, 3},
    {4, 5, 6},
}
```

Slices are references to an underlying array — multiple slices can share the same backing array. Use `copy` when you need an independent copy.

